<ContentPage title="AI Readiness & Governance" eyebrow="TechSafeAI capability" intro="Identify where AI may add value while defining authority, information security, human review and operating controls before automation expands." backHref="/solutions" backLabel="Solutions">
<section class="content-section"><div class="shell content-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow">What this route addresses</div><h2>Start with the operating issue.</h2><p>Technology is selected only after the problem, authority, information boundary and desired outcome are understood.</p></div><div class="indexed-list"><div class="indexed-item"><span class="index">01</span><div><h3>Start with workflow pain</h3><p>Use AI only where a real operating problem and value hypothesis exist.</p></div></div><div class="indexed-item"><span class="index">02</span><div><h3>Set authority boundaries</h3><p>Define what AI may assist with and what remains human-only.</p></div></div><div class="indexed-item"><span class="index">03</span><div><h3>Protect information</h3><p>Resolve data classification, processing and access expectations before protected information moves.</p></div></div><div class="indexed-item"><span class="index">04</span><div><h3>Define verification</h3><p>Require a method for checking outputs, adoption and value rather than assuming AI performance.</p></div></div></div></div></section>
</ContentPage>
